# CODEOWNERS — the ownership half of the selective code-owner review gate
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# The standard: musher-dev/platform ADR 0134, checked by engineering-conventions
# COMM-09 (no `*` catch-all) and COMM-10 (every anchored path exists). The
# other half: .github/rulesets/main-branch.json (`require_code_owner_review`).
#
# How review works here:
#
#   A pull request that touches NO path listed below merges on green CI alone:
#   the required checks are the gate. That includes Dependabot's Feature,
#   action and stack-image bumps, which the frozen-lockfile build and the
#   toolchain verification check, not a reviewer.
#   A pull request that touches a listed path also needs its owner's approval.
#   GitHub waives that on the owner's own pull requests.
#
# What is owned, and why:
#   /.github/          the gate itself: this file, the rulesets, the workflows
#                      that run the required checks, the Dependabot config
#   /.repo/            the declarations, the waivers that silence this
#                      repository's own findings, and the `repo` policies
#   /.devcontainer/features/mise/
#                      the local Feature that downloads and installs mise as
#                      root in every repository built from this container
#   /.devcontainer/scripts/
#                      the lifecycle scripts every repository's container runs,
#                      including the GitHub credential and npm registry setup
#
# Everything else is unowned on purpose. Pin and lock files
# (.devcontainer/devcontainer.json's Features, devcontainer-lock.json,
# .config/mise/, the stack compose files) stay unowned so bot pull requests
# merge on green CI. Listing a path is a commitment to review every change to
# it, so keep the list short.
#
# Syntax rules that bite:
#   - NEVER add a `*` catch-all (COMM-09). It makes every pull request
#     codeowned and brings back blanket review of the whole repository.
#   - LAST matching pattern wins — order from broad to specific.
#   - ALL owners for a pattern go on ONE line.
#   - Owners need EXPLICIT write access to this repo, or the entry is silently
#     ignored and the path becomes unowned. GitHub lists such lines at
#     `gh api repos/musher-dev/development-container/codeowners/errors`.
#   - A root-anchored path must exist (COMM-10): after a rename, the old line
#     protects nothing.

/.github/                         @musher-dev/engineering
/.repo/                           @musher-dev/engineering
/.devcontainer/features/mise/     @musher-dev/engineering
/.devcontainer/scripts/           @musher-dev/engineering
